          "advisory": {
            "id": "RUSTSEC-2026-0386",
            "package": "tokio",
            "title": "`AsyncFd::new` and related constructors violate I/O safety",
            "description": "`tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd` provides safe constructors (`new`, `with_interest`, `try_new`, and `try_with_interest`) that accept any `T: AsRawFd` rather than requiring proof of ownership or validity of the file descriptor. Because `RawFd` implements `AsRawFd`, safe code can construct an `AsyncFd` from an arbitrary or closed file descriptor, or close/replace the underlying file descriptor while the `AsyncFd` is still alive.\r\n\r\nThis violates I/O safety in two ways:\r\n\r\n1. `AsyncFd<T>` implements `AsFd` for all `T: AsRawFd` by calling `BorrowedFd::borrow_raw(self.as_raw_fd())`, allowing safe code to obtain an arbitrary `BorrowedFd<'_>` without owning the file descriptor.\r\n2. Tokio's I/O driver stores a pointer to an internal allocation in the `epoll`/`kqueue` user data for registered file descriptors. If the underlying file descriptor is duplicated and then closed while an `AsyncFd` is alive, and the OS reuses that file descriptor number for a another IO resource on the same runtime, dropping the first `AsyncFd` deregisters the reused file descriptor number and frees the first while the original file description remains registered in `epoll`, leading to a use-after-free when a readiness event fires.\r\n\r\nStarting in Tokio 1.51.6, 1.53.3, and 1.54.0, `AsyncFd::new`, `AsyncFd::with_interest`, `AsyncFd::try_new`, and `AsyncFd::try_with_interest` are deprecated in favor of the `unsafe` constructors `AsyncFd::register` and `AsyncFd::register_with_interest`. Callers must ensure that the file descriptor remains valid, open, and unchanged for the lifetime of the `AsyncFd`.",
            "date": "2026-10-13",
            "aliases": [],
            "related": [],
            "collection": "crates",
            "categories": [
              "memory-corruption"
            ],
            "keywords": [
              "io-safety",
              "use-after-free"
            ],
            "cvss": null,
            "informational": "unsound",
            "references": [
              "https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/issues/8538",
              "https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/issues/8539"
            ],
            "source": null,
            "url": "https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8587",
            "withdrawn": null,
            "license": "CC0-1.0",
            "expect-deleted": false
          },
          "affected": {
            "arch": [],
            "os": [],
            "functions": {
              "tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::new": [
                ">=0.3.2"
              ],
              "tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::try_new": [
                ">=1.37.0"
              ],
              "tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::try_with_interest": [
                ">=1.37.0"
              ],
              "tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::with_interest": [
